        "public_conclusion": "In the A-A section, the slender unhatched band left of the main vertical bore is bounded by two parallel solid lines with a dash-dot centerline, has hatched solid material on BOTH sides (a hatched wall separates it from the left exterior surface), starts at the top phi4 cross-hole (shown with drill-cone X intersection) and runs down to the bottom base cavity — the classic longitudinal-section appearance of a small internal drilled hole, not a surface groove."
